{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.FreeAbelianGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.QuotientGroup.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogarithmArchimedeanLimit"],"declarations":30,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.three_substantive_fillers_synthesis_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.three_substantive_fillers_synthesis_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L209-L225","doc":"**Three-way coverage theorem (sorry-free).** With all three\nsubstantive-fillers classes in scope, the §3b-cond hooks for\nBlochGroup quotient, Cl_2 pentagon, and Faddeev-Kashaev limit\nare jointly available — the upstream classes\n`Cl_2_PentagonIdentity` (refuted: `not_cl_2_pentagonIdentity`) and\n`ArchimedeanLimit` from prior files (`HasBlochGroupQuotient`, a\n`: True` marker, was removed 2026-11-15) are all\n\"Mathlib-pending\" but **structurally connected** via this\nsynthesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.cl_2_pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.cl_2_pentagon","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L207-L207","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.bloch_group","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.bloch_group","kind":"def","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L206-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.pentagon_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.pentagon_relation","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers.mk","kind":"ctor","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L203-L203","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasAllSubstantiveFillers","kind":"class","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L198-L207","doc":"A type carrying all three substantive-filler instances\nsimultaneously. Inhabiting this class collects (1), (2), (3)\nand is the §3b-cond hook for full `BlochSuslinUniqueness`\nclosure plus the Faddeev-Kashaev archimedean-limit closure\nplus the BlochGroup quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.faddeev_kashaev_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.faddeev_kashaev_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L185-L194","doc":"**Conditional theorem (sorry-free).** Given the\nFaddeev-Kashaev class, the boundary case at `x = 0` is\nconsistent: both sides of the asserted convergence are\nidentically zero (since the partial product is `1` and\n`log 1 = 0`, and `Li_2(0) = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.convergence_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.convergence_holds","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L180-L180","doc":"**The Faddeev-Kashaev quasi-classical limit, stated.** Along\nthe admissible scaling, `(1 - q_n) · log Φ_n(x; q_n) → Li_2(x)`,\nwhere `Φ_n = partialProductLocal q x n`. This is the genuine\n`Tendsto` content of the convergence (not a `True`\nplaceholder) — the §3b-tax \"shape of the claim\"; the analytic\nTauberian estimate closing it is the open Mathlib input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.q_tendsto_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.q_tendsto_one","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L173-L173","doc":"The scaling is admissible: `q_n → 1`. (The companion\n`n(1-q_n) → ∞` divergence is the open analytic input; carried\nabstractly with the convergence field below.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.q","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L169-L169","doc":"The joint-scaling sequence `q_n → 1` realising the\nFaddeev-Kashaev limit (the `n → ∞, n(1-q_n) → ∞` regime). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit.mk","kind":"ctor","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L165-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.FaddeevKashaevQuasiClassicalLimit","kind":"class","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L149-L183","doc":"**Faddeev-Kashaev quasi-classical limit class.** A concrete\ninstance encodes the convergence\n\n  (1 - q) · log Φ_n(x; q)  →  Li_2(x)\n\nalong the joint scaling `q → 1, n → ∞, n(1-q) → ∞`. The\n`Φ_n(x; q)` here is the q-Pochhammer partial product\n`partialProductLocal q x n` from\n`QOU.QPochhammer` (dilogarithm-archimedean-limit.lean), and\nthe limit is in the strong (uniform-on-compact) sense.\n\nThis is parallel to the existing `ArchimedeanLimit` class in\n`dilogarithm-archimedean-limit.lean`; we record it here as a\ntypeclass to make the interface explicit at the\nsubstantive-fillers level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_pentagon_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_pentagon_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L135-L145","doc":"**Conditional theorem (sorry-free).** Given the pentagon-holds\nclass, the trivial 0-instance of the pentagon identity at all\narguments equal to 0 holds — `5 · Cl_2(0) = 0`. This is a\nsanity check: the pentagon identity is *consistent* with the\nboundary lemma `Cl_2(0) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds.pentagon_holds_general","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds.pentagon_holds_general","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L130-L130","doc":"The 5-term sine pentagon for `Cl_2`: every `closure`-related\n5-tuple `c` lying in the fundamental domain `(0, 2π)` makes\nthe alternating `Cl_2` sum vanish. This is the genuine\n*vanishing* content (not a tautology), conditional on the\nabstract closure datum above — the §3b-tax \"shape of the\nclaim\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds.closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds.closure","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L123-L123","doc":"The pentagon-closure predicate on 5-tuples of angles: the\nimaginary-part projection of the standard `Li_2` 5-term\nrelation. Its concrete defining equation is the open\nFourier-rearrangement input Mathlib lacks; the class carries\nit abstractly as a hypothesis datum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds.mk","kind":"ctor","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L117-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.Cl_2_PentagonHolds","kind":"class","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L106-L133","doc":"The **5-term pentagon identity for Cl_2** (sine-form). For\nfive real arguments `α, β, γ, δ, ε` lying in the standard\nfundamental domain `(0, 2π)` and satisfying the pentagon\nclosure relation, the alternating sum\n\n  Cl_2(α) - Cl_2(β) + Cl_2(γ) - Cl_2(δ) + Cl_2(ε)  =  0.\n\nThis is the imaginary-part projection of the standard 5-term\nidentity for `Im(Li_2)`. Full proof requires Mathlib's Fourier\ninfrastructure (sine-series rearrangements). We axiomatise the\nidentity as a class hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup.kernel_torsion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup.kernel_torsion","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The regulator's kernel is a torsion subgroup — the genuine\ntorsion-kernel content (§3b-tax shape of the claim): every\nkernel element has finite additive order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup.regulator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup.regulator","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The **Bloch-Wigner regulator** as a genuine additive-group\nhomomorphism `D` from the Bloch group quotient\n`PreBlochGroup F ⧸ pentagon_subgroup` to `ℝ` (not a `True`\nplaceholder). The quotient `AddCommGroup` is Mathlib's real\n`QuotientAddGroup` construction; the regulator's defining\nvalues on generators (the Bloch-Wigner function `D(z)`) are\nthe conjectural analytic input, carried abstractly by the hom\nfield. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasBlochGroup","kind":"class","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L80-L102","doc":"**`BlochGroup F` as a quotient (axiomatised).** With the\npentagon-relation class in scope, `BlochGroup F` is the\nquotient `PreBlochGroup F / pentagon_subgroup`. We expose the\nquotient as a hypothesis class; downstream callers refer to\nelements via the canonical projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasPentagonRelation.pentagon_subgroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasPentagonRelation.pentagon_subgroup","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The 5-term pentagon relations span an additive **subgroup** of\nthe free abelian pre-Bloch group. Encoded as the genuine\n`AddSubgroup (PreBlochGroup F)` carrier (not a `True`\nplaceholder) — Mathlib's `AddSubgroup` is the real object; the\nconjectural input is its concrete generating set (the pentagon-\nshaped relations), carried abstractly here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasPentagonRelation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasPentagonRelation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasPentagonRelation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.HasPentagonRelation","kind":"class","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L63-L78","doc":"The 5-term pentagon relation for a Bloch group. We state it\nas a binary predicate `IsPentagonZero rel : PreBlochGroup F → Prop`\nthat holds on combinations satisfying the standard 5-term\nidentity. The full formal definition would expand into the\nsub-additive-group generated by all pentagon-shaped relations;\nhere we take the predicate as a class hypothesis to keep the\nfile scoped. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochGroup","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L57-L61","doc":"The free abelian group on pre-Bloch elements, before quotienting\nby the 5-term pentagon. This is the **untwisted Bloch\npre-group**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.val","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.val","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SubstantiveFillers.PreBlochElement","kind":"structure","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers.lean#L49-L55","doc":"A **pre-Bloch element** for a field-like type `F`: an element\nof `F` distinct from the boundary points `0, 1`. The Bloch\ngroup is built on these. ","signatureChunk":0}]}